selector_to_html = {"a[href=\"ThrustChamberComponent.html#pyskyfire.viz.components.ThrustChamberComponent\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.components.ThrustChamberComponent\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.viz.components.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">ThrustChamberComponent</span></span></dt><dd><p>Cooling-channel surfaces with optional RegenResult fields.</p><p>Each layout seed is constructed once. Instances share its immutable mesh\nand fields and carry separate rotations and identities. No hot wall is\nconstructed. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">circuit_N.inlet/outlet</span></code> anchors refer to the first seed\u2019s\nfirst channel, at its end-section polygon centre, not a manifold port.\nEvery channel also exposes its own inlet/outlet anchors.</p><p>A circuit with a result records its coolant\u2019s CoolProp name as\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">metadata[\"fluid\"]</span></code>. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">circuit_colors</span></code> paints each circuit apart;\nwithout it every channel takes the default colour.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#module-pyskyfire.viz.components\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.viz.components<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.viz.components\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>Engineering objects adapted into local-coordinate scene hierarchies.</p>", "a[href=\"#module-contents\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Module Contents<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-contents\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"#functions\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Functions<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#functions\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"TurbineComponent.html#pyskyfire.viz.components.TurbineComponent\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.components.TurbineComponent\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.viz.components.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">TurbineComponent</span></span></dt><dd><p>Display a built turbine: its passage walls and every row\u2019s blades.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">geometry</span></code> is a <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">TurbineGeometry</span></code>. Walls are\nthe passage revolved about the local +x shaft; each row\u2019s one built blade\nis repeated round the wheel in the turbine\u2019s rotation sense. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">colors</span></code>\npaints (stator, rotor) blades apart; without it every part takes the\ndefault colour. Optional <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">results</span></code> maps part names\n(hub, shroud, <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">&lt;row&gt;_&lt;i&gt;</span></code>) to dictionaries of mesh-aligned FieldData.\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">inlet</span></code> and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">outlet</span></code> anchors sit on the axis at the passage ends,\npointing out of the turbine.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"ImpellerComponent.html#pyskyfire.viz.components.ImpellerComponent\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.components.ImpellerComponent\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.viz.components.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">ImpellerComponent</span></span></dt><dd><p>Display prepared impeller.geometry arrays, with the existing local x shaft axis.</p><p>Optional <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">results</span></code> maps part names (hub, shroud, blade_N) to dictionaries\nof mesh-aligned FieldData. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">inlet</span></code> and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">shaft</span></code> are axial centre datums;\nthere is no discrete outlet port on a radially discharging impeller.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"AnnularDuctComponent.html#pyskyfire.viz.components.AnnularDuctComponent\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.components.AnnularDuctComponent\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.viz.components.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">AnnularDuctComponent</span></span></dt><dd><p>Display an <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">AnnularDuct</span></code>.</p><p>The duct is drawn as its hub and shroud revolved about the local +x\nshaft, with <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">inlet</span></code> and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">outlet</span></code> anchors on the axis at its ends as a\nturbine\u2019s are. The shroud is translucent so the hub shows. A pipe with a\ncore is drawn by <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">PipeComponent</span></code>.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">results</span></code> is a <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">DuctResult</span></code>, or a mapping of\nfield names to FieldData with one value per station (point) or per\ninterval (cell). Both walls carry the same fields.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.viz.components.duct_fields\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.components.duct_fields\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.viz.components.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">duct_fields</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">result</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Adapt a <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">DuctResult</span></code> into scene fields.</p><p>Station quantities become point fields and interval (connection)\nquantities become cell fields, both in the base SI units the solver\nalready works in. NaN is retained where an interval does not define a\nquantity, such as the Darcy factor of a lumped bend. <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"PipeComponent.html#pyskyfire.viz.components.PipeComponent\" title=\"pyskyfire.viz.components.PipeComponent\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">PipeComponent</span></code></a>\nand <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"AnnularDuctComponent.html#pyskyfire.viz.components.AnnularDuctComponent\" title=\"pyskyfire.viz.components.AnnularDuctComponent\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">AnnularDuctComponent</span></code></a> map either association onto their\nmeshes.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"VoluteComponent.html#pyskyfire.viz.components.VoluteComponent\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.components.VoluteComponent\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.viz.components.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">VoluteComponent</span></span></dt><dd><p>Display a resolved volute or collector passage.</p><p>The volute supplies its own geometry through <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">sweep(n_points=...)</span></code>, which\nplaces each station\u2019s cross-section in machine coordinates, already\ninclined by the volute\u2019s tilt. The local frame is that frame: the machine\naxis is +z, the tongue sits at azimuth zero, and no recentering is applied.</p><p>The passage is swept from the tongue through one revolution, and on through\nits <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">ExitCone</span></code> duct to the flange when it has one.\nThe face at the tongue is a wall \u2013 the cutwater \u2013 so the step visible\nthere is the passage meeting itself.</p><p>Three child nodes come back, so the openings can be told apart from the\nwalls at a glance:</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">opening_color</span></code> paints both openings, red by default. They carry no\nfields, so they keep that colour whichever field the scene is coloured by,\nrather than disappearing into the scale.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">results</span></code> is a <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">VoluteResult</span></code>, or a mapping of\nfield names to point-associated FieldData with one value per azimuthal\nstation. A supplied mapping holds its last value along the exit cone, which\na result does only for quantities that have no variation to carry there.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"ManifoldComponent.html#pyskyfire.viz.components.ManifoldComponent\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.components.ManifoldComponent\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.viz.components.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">ManifoldComponent</span></span></dt><dd><p>Display a resolved distributing or collecting manifold.</p><p>The manifold supplies its own geometry through <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">sweep(n_points=...)</span></code>,\nalready placed on the wall it was built against, and the local frame is\nthat frame: the machine axis is +z and the dead point sits at azimuth zero.\nA split manifold sweeps the whole ring, both branches together.</p><p>Three child nodes come back, so the opening can be told apart from the\nwalls at a glance:</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">opening_color</span></code> paints only those faces, red by default: the places flow\ncrosses the boundary, not the walls that carry it there. They hold no\nfields, so they keep that colour whichever field the scene is coloured by,\nrather than disappearing into the scale.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">results</span></code> is a mapping of field names to point-associated FieldData, one\nvalue per swept station of the resolved ring \u2013 which for a split manifold\nis both branches, not one.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">n_points</span></code> samples each boundary piece of the section. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">n_stations</span></code>\nrefines the ring in azimuth for drawing, which is the direction a manifold\nfacets in first, and leaves the resolved design alone; values on the\nresolved grid are read between its stations onto the refined mesh. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></code>\ndraws the ring exactly as it was resolved.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"DiffuserComponent.html#pyskyfire.viz.components.DiffuserComponent\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.components.DiffuserComponent\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.viz.components.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">DiffuserComponent</span></span></dt><dd><p>Display a built vaned diffuser: its two walls and every vane.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">diffuser.build_geometry()</span></code> must have been called. The diffuser is drawn\nin the impeller\u2019s own frame, walls symmetric about the impeller outlet\nmid-plane at local x = 0, so it takes the impeller\u2019s rotation and a\ntranslation to that mid-plane. The <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">outlet</span></code> anchor is not a port: the\ndiffuser discharges radially all round into its volute.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.viz.components.volute_fields\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.components.volute_fields\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.viz.components.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">volute_fields</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">result</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">exit_stations</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Adapt a <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">VoluteResult</span></code> into scene fields.</p><p>Every quantity carries one value per azimuthal station, so all are\npoint-associated and <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"VoluteComponent.html#pyskyfire.viz.components.VoluteComponent\" title=\"pyskyfire.viz.components.VoluteComponent\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">VoluteComponent</span></code></a> repeats each around its\nstation\u2019s section ring. Units are the base SI units the solver works in.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">collected</span></code> marks the fraction of the mass flow gathered so far, and\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">clipped</span></code> flags the stations near the tongue where the area law asked for\na section smaller than the family admits.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">exit_stations</span></code> appends that many further values covering the exit-cone\nduct, so a component sweeping the duct can colour it too. Pressure and\nvelocity carry their real variation along it; the rest hold their\ncollection-plane value, since the duct has no azimuth left to vary with.</p><p>The two pressures are worth reading with their model in mind. Aungier\ncharges one lumped coefficient per mechanism across the whole passage, so\nhow the loss is spread round the volute is an assumption made for display\n\u2013 see <code class=\"xref py py-meth docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">stagnation_pressure()</span></code>. The\nendpoints are what the analysis actually fixes.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"PipeComponent.html#pyskyfire.viz.components.PipeComponent\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.components.PipeComponent\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.viz.components.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">PipeComponent</span></span></dt><dd><p>Display an explicitly defined pipe; never route or modify a solver model.</p><p>The pipe supplies its own geometry. A <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Pipe</span></code> offers\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">display_path(segments=...)</span></code>, which opens its rounded and continuous bend\nconnections into arcs for drawing without touching the solved model;\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">segments</span></code> sets the drawn sides per quarter turn. Any other object is read through <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">centerline</span></code>, an (N,3)\nCartesian polyline in metres, and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">radius</span></code>, a positive scalar or one\nradius per station, and is drawn exactly as supplied. The local frame is\nthe frame of those coordinates (no implicit recentering).</p><p>A pipe with a core is drawn as a <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">\"core\"</span></code> surface, one per stretch the\ncore runs along, inside a translucent <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">\"bore\"</span></code> of <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">opacity</span></code>, both\nchildren of the returned node, which carries the bore\u2019s end anchors.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">results</span></code> is a <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">DuctResult</span></code>, or a mapping of\nfield names to FieldData: point-associated with one value per station, or\ncell-associated with one value per connection. Station values are\ninterpolated along refined bends and repeated around each ring; connection\nvalues fill the rings spanning that connection. Every surface carries the\nsame fields.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#classes\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Classes<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#classes\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>"}
skip_classes = ["headerlink", "sd-stretched-link"]

window.onload = function () {
    for (const [select, tip_html] of Object.entries(selector_to_html)) {
        const links = document.querySelectorAll(` ${select}`);
        for (const link of links) {
            if (skip_classes.some(c => link.classList.contains(c))) {
                continue;
            }

            tippy(link, {
                content: tip_html,
                allowHTML: true,
                arrow: true,
                placement: 'auto-start', maxWidth: 600, interactive: false,
                onShow(instance) {MathJax.typesetPromise([instance.popper]).then(() => {});},
            });
        };
    };
    console.log("tippy tips loaded!");
};
